Decision rule (crisp): During peak treat any YELLOW as a mandatory PAUSE (do not advance) to run extended synthetics and a 15–30 minute stabilization window; only resume if synthetics show no merchant‑visible degradation (payment success ≥99.9% and p95 trending back toward baseline) and the p95/error ratio returns to GREEN; escalate to Sev‑2 and consider rollback immediately if the Sev‑2 rule fires (p95 >30% over baseline for 15m) or if RED hard‑fail thresholds are hit (p95 >250ms, error ≥0.1%, or payment success <99.7%) or if merchants complain.  
PromQL / alert pseudo‑expressions (examples): 
- p95_now = histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job="payments-api",env="prod"}[5m])) by (le)); 
- p95_7d = avg_over_time(histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job="payments-api",env="prod"}[5m])) by (le))[7d:5m]); 
- p95_ratio = p95_now / p95_7d; ALERT YELLOW if p95_ratio > 1.05 and p95_ratio <= 1.30 for 5m → pause; ALERT SEV‑2 if p95_ratio > 1.30 for 15m; 
- error_rate = sum(rate(http_requests_total{job="payments-api",env="prod",status=~"5.."}[5m])) / sum(rate(http_requests_total{job="payments-api",env="prod"}[5m])); ALERT RED if error_rate * 100 >= 0.1% for 1m; ALERT YELLOW if error_rate > baseline*1.5 and <0.1%.  
Ticket note templates: 
- Hold (use when pausing): "HOLD @ 5% canary — YELLOW triggered: p95 +20% vs 7d (current X ms), error rate 2.5x baseline (current Y% but <0.1%). Running extended synthetics (20 runs) and 15m stabilization; SRE Lead & RM notified; will update ticket with synthetic results before any further action." 
- Proceed (use when resuming): "PROCEED to next stage — after 15m pause synthetics passed (20/20), p95 reduced to +8% vs 7d and error rate trending to baseline; SRE Lead + RM approve ramp to 25%."
